# GLM-5.3-Flash, ABLITERATED, EXL3 TR3 4-bit, on native TensorFold across both
# Sparks (TP 2, one rank per Spark). 320B total / 18B active, 175.7 GB of
# weights in 83 shards.
#
# What it is: Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-4bpw-TensorFold @ 078455ff (the
# TR3 layout TensorFold's glm5_next engine was tested on: bits 4, codebook
# mcg, scope glm53_routed_experts_only, head_bits 16) with an o_proj
# transplant from an abliterated donor in layers 15-46 (44 skipped, MTP
# layer included): 30 BF16 tensors edited, 30 shards touched. Its own
# ABLIT_VERIFY.json: ok, 30 edited tensors differ, 97 anchors identical,
# 53 untouched shards checked. Max's copy, staged on spark-1 2026-11-13 and
# copied to spark-2 over the ConnectX link.
#
# Why this one over the planned neko-legends/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-EXL3
# (glm53-flash-unc-exl3-tensorfold): it is the variant Max already ran
# across two Sparks, it is local (no gated download), and its base is the
# TensorFold-tested checkpoint itself rather than a same-layout twin.
#
# A local SOURCE has no Hub revision to pin. model-fetch.sh --profile records
# a lock of every file's sha256 on the first run (trust on first use, on
# spark-1, where the copy came from) — commit models/<name>.lock; the second
# Spark's copy must then match it exactly.
BACKEND=tensorfold
SOURCE=/home/max/openbeast-models/glm53-flash-ablit-exl3
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash-ablit
# The native glm5_next engine on EXL3 runs at exactly two ranks.
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=2
# VERIFY ON HARDWARE: TensorFold prints the window it admits at start
# ("N streams at once, … at a W-token window"). Its GLM recipe ran NVFP4 at
# 245760 on two GB10s; EXL3 is ~80 GB/rank lighter on experts, so start there
# and raise once the startup line shows room.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=245760
TENSORFOLD_PARALLEL=auto
